cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use osmo_refdb, or a database release built with it, please cite it
  as below. A release is built from the sources under `references`; cite those
  too, as the release's CC BY 4.0 licence requires (see the README).
type: software
title: osmo_refdb
abstract: >-
  Builds and benchmarks the reference database that osmotool profiles with:
  DIAMOND databases, HMMs with gathering cutoffs and an annotated gene catalogue
  for osmoadaptation gene families.
authors:
  - family-names: Verhaar
    given-names: Barbara
repository-code: https://github.com/barbarahelena/osmo_refdb
license: MIT
keywords:
  - osmoadaptation
  - metagenomics
  - reference database
  - gene catalogue
  - HMM
  - DIAMOND

# The code is MIT. A release (the data) is CC-BY-4.0, with attribution to the
# sources below.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - name: The UniProt Consortium
    title: "UniProt: the Universal Protein Knowledgebase in 2025"
    journal: Nucleic Acids Research
    volume: 53
    issue: D1
    start: D609
    end: D617
    year: 2025
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gkae1010
    notes: Source of the reference sequences, and so of the HMMs and the DIAMOND database.

